From 7cfd764b33253b6b4dcb84ee3636f7104fc1b5e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:04:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] Terrain longwave from air temperature, Hay-Davies
 diffuse, terrain-reflected shortwave

- toposcale.LW_terrain_temperature: air (default), fixed (273.15 K, as
  before) or a value in K. The terrain emitted 0 degC longwave whatever the
  season, too much for cold snow-covered terrain.
- toposcale.diffuse_model: isotropic (default) or hay_davies: the
  circumsolar share of the diffuse (anisotropy index direct / TOA) follows
  the beam on the slope and is shaded with it.
- toposcale.SW_terrain_albedo: the terrain seen by the point (1 - svf)
  reflects the global radiation of a level surface at the point; added to
  SW_diffuse and stored as SW_terrain. 0 (default) is off.

ClimateDownscaler takes the terrain temperature and the albedo as
DataArrays (point_name, time) too: the hook for surface temperatures and
albedos of a snow model run on the points. The output store records the
options in its attributes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
